@page "/docs/api-reference/userinfo"
@layout DocsLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>UserInfo — Vaultex API</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-eyebrow">API reference</div>
<h1>UserInfo</h1>
<p class="docs-lead">
    Returns claims about the user identified by an access token. Useful when your client doesn't
    receive an ID token, or when you need fresh claims after profile updates.
</p>

<div class="docs-endpoint">
    <span class="docs-method docs-method--get">GET</span>
    <span>/connect/userinfo</span>
</div>

<h2 id="auth">Authentication</h2>
<p>Send a valid access token in the <code>Authorization</code> header.</p>

<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">HTTP</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>GET /connect/userinfo HTTP/1.1
Host: auth.vaultex.io
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOi...</code></pre>
</div>

<h2 id="response">Response</h2>
<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">JSON</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>{
  "sub":            "f3a7d2c9-1b4e-4f0a-9c2e-1234567890ab",
  "name":           "Sarah Chen",
  "preferred_username": "sarah",
  "email":          "sarah@example.com",
  "email_verified": true,
  "tid":            "acme",
  "role":           ["Admin", "Viewer"]
}</code></pre>
</div>

<p>Which claims you receive depends on the scopes the access token was issued with. See <a href="/docs/concepts/scopes-claims">Scopes &amp; claims</a>.</p>

<h2 id="errors">Errors</h2>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>401 Unauthorized</code></td><td>Missing, expired, or invalid access token.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>403 Forbidden</code></td><td>Token lacks the <code>openid</code> scope.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

